You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Liquid Fill Text (`text-liquid-fill`)

Outlined letters as glass vessels: two offset waves slosh inside the type (SVG clip to the text) and rise to a level you control — loaders, counters, scroll progress.

## What it should do
Build liquid-fill text in SVG: a clipPath of the text; inside it a group translated by (100 − level) that contains two seamless wave paths (period 50, tile 200) looping horizontally in opposite directions with animateTransform; draw an outlined copy of the text on top. Ease level changes with a CSS transition.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **svg**.
- No runtime dependencies (CSS only).
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/text-liquid-fill.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** role=img with an aria-label that includes the percentage. Reduced motion: still waves, level jumps.
- **Performance:** Pure SVG: two SMIL translate loops and one CSS transform transition.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

